    <details><summary>Why does my internet speed change between tests?</summary><div class="faq-answer"><p>Results can vary with Wi-Fi signal, active devices, provider congestion, test-server load and routing. Repeat tests under similar conditions and compare a few results instead of relying on one reading.</p></div></details>
    <details><summary>Is download speed the only number that matters?</summary><div class="faq-answer"><p>No. Download and upload speed describe throughput, while ping and jitter help explain response time and consistency. The most useful measurements depend on what you are doing online.</p></div></details>
    <details><summary>Why is Wi-Fi slower in another room?</summary><div class="faq-answer"><p>Distance, walls, floors and wireless interference can weaken the connection. Compare a test near your router with one from the problem room, using the same device.</p></div></details>
    <details><summary>Can a speed test guarantee gaming or video-call quality?</summary><div class="faq-answer"><p>No single test can guarantee every service's performance. Server route, latency, jitter, packet loss and the service itself can all affect real-time applications.</p></div></details>
